    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1448" root="او" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوٌّ</span></b>  The <i>word</i> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْ</span></b>  <i>when made a noun.</i> (T, K.) So
say the grammarians. (T.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذهِ أَوٌّحَسَنَةٌ</span>
[<i>This is a good</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْ</span>]. (T.) And to one who uses
the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْعَلُ كَذَا أَوْ كَذَا</span>, (T,) you say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَعِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَوَّجَانِبًا</span> [<i>Let thou,</i> or <i>leave thou, the word</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْ</span>
<i>alone</i>]. (T, K.)

